--
-- Hand-maintained video fixtures for bill pages.
--
-- Unlike video-records.sql (which deploy/database_export.sh regenerates), this file is maintained
-- by hand. It gives two 2025 bills real, captioned video so the bill-page video player and
-- transcript can be developed and tested locally and in CI:
--
--   SB738 (2025), two clips in two different files:
--     1. Senate floor, April 2, 2025: the vote on the governor's amendments.
--     2. School Health Services Subcommittee, September 15, 2025: a witness discussing the effect
--        of the cell phone law that SB738 created. (Chosen to exercise multi-file playback.)
--   SB805 (2025), one clip:
--     1. Senate floor, April 2, 2025: debate on the governor's amendments.
--
-- Transcript lines are taken verbatim from each file's WebVTT captions, split into speaker turns
-- at the captions' ">>" markers. Speaker IDs are terms.id values (530 = Pekarsky, 342 = Surovell).
--
-- The Senate's live captions trail the audio, so each clip's caption times have been moved earlier
-- by that clip's measured lag (the median gap between each caption and when its words are spoken,
-- per Whisper word timings): 7.2s and 6.5s for the April 2 clips, 6.4s for September 15.
--
-- Rows use INSERT IGNORE so that, when local-test-records.sql has already loaded the full `files`
-- rows, those are kept.
--

